2026-06-13 chore/rename-momentum-season-record — CPO §10 NAMING ruling on the form-window model family. The family used three roots for one concept (form_window + momentum + the literal last_5) while the season concept used season_to_date; builder asked which consistent vocabulary to adopt and presented Option 1 (momentum + season_to_date) vs Option 2 (momentum + season_record). Builder opinion: Option 2 — `season_record` matches the metrics_context_model.md §1 concept word ("Season record") and describes the builder's full role (yields to-date / full-season / year-over-year), where "season_to_date" names only one cut. CPO RULING (conversation, 2026-06-13): "I tend to Option 2 … Go." → adopt `momentum` + `season_record`. Refinement (builder, accepted in the same exchange): the `window_type` VALUES (`last_5`, `season_to_date`, `prev_season`) are a SEPARATE axis (the cut, not the model root) and stay window-descriptive; the published JSON output key `form_window` is the UI contract and is NOT renamed (only mart TABLE-NAME reads change). Pure rename — no SQL logic/grain/metric change. Recorded here so the contract's decisions_taken cites a locatable ruling.

